// mgd_smooth.glslinc — one Jacobi relaxation of A_L u = rhs at level L, STAMP-GENERIC.
//
// Fork of mg_smooth.glslinc for MgDeepSolver (solver-ledger.md §7a). mg_smooth is left
// alone — it still backs MgvSolver, which stays in the dropdown as the uniform-beta
// control. The whole difference is these two lines:
//
//     mg_smooth :  diag = 1 + a + aMu*(leak + 4*pc.beta)   <- ONE scalar beta, everywhere
//     mgd_smooth:  diag = st_diag(c)                        <- the stamp's operator
//
// so a bed ramp / per-face depth / sponge / DC mode all reach the smoother instead of
// being flattened to a constant. That is the entire point of the fork: at extra.z > 0
// mg_smooth is inverting a DIFFERENT matrix from the one Jacobi/RBGS/CG invert.
//
// Level scaling is NOT in this file. The host hands each level the stamp's own push
// constant with `size` and `beta_scale` (and `sponge_w`) rewritten, and st_depth()
// re-derives per-face conductance from that size on its own — so no Galerkin coarsening.
//
// Host must compile as: "#version 450" + local_size + THIS header block + stamp + body.
// The stamp declares h_curr (set 0) / h_prev (set 1) and `pc`; neither is read here
// (st_diag and st_conductance are pure functions of pc), but both must still be bound.

void main() {
    ST_IVEC c = ST_CELL();
    if (ST_OOB(c)) {
        return;
    }

    float acc = imageLoad(rhs_img, c).r;
    for (int k = 0; k < ST_NB; k++) {
        ST_IVEC n = ST_NEIGHBOUR(c, k);
        acc += st_conductance(c, n) * imageLoad(u_in, n).r;
    }
    imageStore(u_out, c, vec4(acc / st_diag(c), 0.0, 0.0, 0.0));
}
